# Raw NSE payloads: 293MB and growing, refetchable via backfill.py.
# The manifests are what make a backtest reproducible, not the bytes.
data/raw/
data/journal.db
data/cron.log

# Keep: holidays.json and judge_ledger.json are derived state that must not be
# silently regenerated -- the ledger is the audit trail of holdout consultations.
!data/holidays.json
!data/judge_ledger.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env

# Upstox instrument master: 9,650 rows, refetchable, changes only with listings.
data/upstox_instruments.json

# --- macOS and editor junk -------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.bak

# --- runtime state: regenerated every agent tick, never read as evidence ---
# These churned in almost every commit and say nothing a reader needs. The
# agent rewrites them constantly; git history of them is noise.
data/agent*.log
data/telegram.log
data/audit.log
data/DIGEST.md
data/agent_state.json
data/agent_heartbeat.json
# Same thing for the listener. Rewritten every ~60s, so tracking it puts a
# one-line diff in every unrelated commit. /health reads the file on disk.
data/listener_heartbeat.json
data/agent.lock
data/tg_offset.json

# --- XBRL filings: 40,775 files, 84% of the repo, and no measured signal ---
# Four company-momentum features across 1,049 randomly sampled trades: every
# confidence interval straddles zero (CLAUDE.md). The score does not read them
# and features.attach_fundamentals treats absence as normal -- 15% of the
# universe has no filings at all.
#
# NOT refetchable while www.nseindia.com blocks us, so the local 1.6GB copy is
# the only one. It stays on disk; this only stops it being pushed.
data/fundamentals/

# Kept deliberately: pbook.db is the record of real forward trades and cannot
# be regenerated from anything. findings/strategies/simulations/walkforward
# jsonl, the baselines and holidays.json are evidence, not runtime state.

# THE LIVE ORDER RECORD, and pre-migration copies of it. Both stay on disk;
# neither is committed. Tracking the binary is what let a `git switch` replace
# the live forward-trade record with another branch's copy -- silently, since a
# checkout says nothing about a file it overwrites, and the diff read only
# "Bin 12288 -> 20480 bytes". data/positions_record.sql is the tracked copy:
# text, so a changed position is a readable diff, written by every daily.py
# tick and checked against the live database by audit.py.
data/positions.db
data/positions.db.bak-*

# Claude Code's config. Tracking it made a local tool setting a repo change,
# and because the sandbox may not write this path a branch switch could not
# check it out -- which is what blocked a fast-forward for three attempts while
# the working tree sat on the wrong version of tg.py. It then happened AGAIN the
# day settings.json and skills/ were added: the merge aborted on "untracked
# working tree files would be overwritten", and the tracked copy could not be
# updated afterwards because the sandbox denies the path -- so the repo held a
# settings.json contradicting the one actually in force.
#
# scripts/claude/ is the reviewable source of truth and one cp installs it,
# exactly like scripts/deploy/. A file this repo cannot write is a file this
# repo must not track.
.claude/

# iCloud conflict copies ("DIGEST 2.md", "agent_state 2.json"). Nothing reads
# them; they are stale snapshots that show up as untracked changes.
* 2.*

# --- NSE corporate announcements: ~770k rows, 0.54GB, refetchable -----------
# Same category as data/fundamentals/ above: a bulk third-party payload that
# backfill() re-fetches on demand and that says nothing a reader of a diff
# needs. The evidence is not the bytes, it is the frozen tone table and the
# measured result.
#
# The two subdirectories are named individually rather than ignoring
# data/announcements/ wholesale, BECAUSE tone_table.json lives beside them and
# must stay tracked: it is the pre-registered category->sign mapping, committed
# before the run that uses it, and a hindsight machine the moment it is
# editable without a diff. Ignoring the parent and negating the file would work
# until someone reordered the rules.
data/announcements/raw/
data/announcements/parsed/

# Forward news capture: append-only, grows daily, regenerated by nothing --
# but it is a running log rather than evidence, and tracking it would put a
# diff in every commit. It stays on disk; losing it costs only the days since
# the last capture, which no backtest can read anyway.
data/news/

# --- local tool caches -------------------------------------------------------
.agents/
.playwright/
.superpowers/
dashboard/
data/screener_raw/
data/fundamentals_screener/
data/fund_annual*.log
data/fund_backfill.log
data/fund_reparse.log
